#* {{quote-text|en|year=1839|title=A Challenge to Phrenologists; Or, Phrenology Tested|page=155
|passage=What can we know of any substance or existence, but as made up of all the qualities that '''go''' to its composition: extension, solidity, form, colour; take these away, and you know nothing.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1907|author=Patrick Doyle|title=Indian Engineering|volume=41|page=181
|passage=The avoirdupois pound is one of 7,000 grains, and '''go''' to the pound.}}
# To [[pass]], to be used up:
