|passage=But the days '''went''' and '''went''', and she never came; and then I thought I would come here where you were.}}
##* {{quote-book|en|year=2008|author=Sue Raymond|title=Hidden Secrets|isbn=1435747070|page=357
|passage=The rest of the morning '''went''' quickly and before Su knew it Jean was knocking on the door {{...}}}}
## {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[end]] or [[disappear]]. {{q|Compare ''[[go away]]''.}}
##: {{syn|en|disappear|vanish|go away|end|dissipate}}
##: {{ant|en|remain|stay|hold}}
##: {{ux|en|After three days, my headache finally '''went'''.}}
