#* {{quote-book|en|year=1978|author={{w|David Galloway (writer)|David Galloway}}|title=A Family Album|location=London|publisher={{w|Calder Publishing|John Calder}}|isbn=0714536822|page=36|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/familyalbumnovel0000gall/page/36/mode/2up?q=go|passage=After two years of swaddled invalidism, Mrs. Morton emitted a final gassy sigh and died, whereas twenty years later Elihu was to '''go''' “just like that,” as the neighbors said, from a stroke.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1997|author=John Wheatcroft|title=The Education of Malcolm Palmer|page=85|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=Khzh-qMNCE8C|isbn=0845348639|passage="Your father's '''gone'''." "Okay, okay, the Gaffer's kicked off. What happened?"}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive|cricket}} To be [[lose|lost]] or [[out]]:
